// Opt-in rebase policy preset.
//
// By default Renovate uses `rebaseWhen: "behind-base-branch"`, which rebases (and
// force-pushes) every open Renovate PR whenever the base branch moves. On high-traffic
// repositories this re-triggers the full CI suite hundreds of times per PR.
//
// This preset only rebases when there is a real merge conflict. PRs that genuinely need to
// stay continuously up to date can opt back in per-PR via the `keep-updated` label, and a
// one-off rebase can be requested via the `rebase` label (Renovate removes it afterwards).
//
// This is intentionally NOT part of the default preset: low-traffic repositories are fine
// with the default behavior. Adopt it only on repositories identified as Renovate-driven CI
// cost hotspots.
{
  $schema: "https://docs.renovatebot.com/renovate-schema.json",
  rebaseWhen: "conflicted",
  rebaseLabel: "rebase",
  keepUpdatedLabel: "keep-updated",
}
